 {Finite energy}

Besides assuming that the image of the map is sufficiently ``small'', another common assumption is the finiteness of the energy. A classical result in this direction is due to Schoen and Yau.

 {theorem}[ {SYau1976ener}]
Let $(M,g)$ be a complete Riemannian manifold with nonnegative Ricci curvature, and let $(N,h)$ be a Riemannian manifold with nonpositive sectional curvature. If $f:M  N$ is a harmonic map with finite energy, then $f$ is constant.
 {theorem}

In addition, Garber, Ruijsenaars, Seiler, and Burns proved in  {Garber1979sigma} that if
\[
