is a harmonic map with finite energy, then $u$ is constant. Subsequently, Hildebrandt and Sealey obtained several generalizations. Hildebrandt showed that the metric on the domain may be replaced by a globally conformally flat metric, while Sealey showed that the domain may be replaced by the Poincar\'e ball $ {D}^m$; see  {Hil1982liou,sealeysome1982}.

